 ⍝ BASIC SIMPLEX METHOD: DETERMINE ONE OR MORE NONEGATIVE VECTORS X
 ⍝ WHICH OPTIMIZE THE OBJECTIVE FUNCTION C+.×X SUBJECT TO CONSTRAINTS:
 ⍝ (((S='≤')⌿A)+.×X)≤(S='≤')/B; (((S='≥')⌿A)+.×X)≥(S='≥')/B; AND
 ⍝ (((S='=')⌿A)+.×X)=(S='=')/B.  THE ARGUMENT U IS EQUAL TO ONE FOR
 ⍝ MAXIMIZATION AND MINUS ONE FOR MINIMIZATION.  A, B, AND C ARE
 ⍝ NUMERIC GLOBAL INPUTS WITH (⍴A) = (⍴B),⍴C.  S IS A CHARACTER GLOBAL
 ⍝ INPUT VECTOR OF SIGNS '≤≥=' WITH (⍴S) = ⍴B.  OTHER NUMERIC GLOBAL
 ⍝ INPUT SCALARS ARE BIGM, WHICH IS A POSITIVE NUMBER SIGNIFICANTLY
 ⍝ LARGER THAN ⌈/|C USED TO FORCE ARTIFICIAL VARIABLES OUT OF THE BASIS,
 ⍝ MAXITER, WHICH LIMITS THE NUMBER OF SIMPLEX ITERATIONS, AND MAXOPT,
 ⍝ WHICH LIMITS THE NUMBER OF ALTERNATIVE OPTIMAL SOLUTIONS. THE
 ⍝ EXPLICIT RESULT K IS EQUAL TO: ZERO IF AN OPTIMAL SOLUTION IS
 ⍝ DETERMINED; ONE IF NO SOLUTION EXISTS; TWO IF THE SOLUTION IS
 ⍝ UNBOUNDED; AND THREE IF THE ITERATION LIMIT IS ACTIVE.  IF AN
 ⍝ OPTIMAL SOLUTION IS DETERMINED, THE ROWS OF PRIMAL CONTAIN ONE OR
 ⍝ MORE DISTINCT ALTERNATIVE PRIMAL SOLUTIONS, THE ROWS OF DUAL CONTAIN
 ⍝ CORRESPONDING (NOT NECESSARILY DISTINCT) DUAL SOLUTIONS, PRIMAL_OBJ
 ⍝ CONTAINS THE OPTIMAL VALUE OF THE PRIMAL OBJECTIVE FUNCTION, AND
 ⍝ DUAL_OBJ CONTAINS THE OPTIMAL VALUE OF THE DUAL OBJECTIVE FUNCTION.
 ⍝ WITH PERFECT ARITHMETIC, WE SHOULD HAVE PRIMAL_OBJ = DUAL_OBJ.
 ⍝ ITERATIONS IS THE TOTAL NUMBER OF CYCLES THROUGH THE MAIN LOOP.
